{
  "dom_id": "step-e7704",
  "name": "Example: Solving an Inequality When the Exponential is Compared to Zero or a Negative Number",
  "problem": "Solve the inequality $4 \\cdot 3^{8-x} + 12 > 0.$",
  "worked_solution": "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\cdot {3}^{8-x}+12 & >0 \\\\ 4\\cdot {3}^{8-x} & >-12 \\\\ {3}^{8-x} & >-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause a power of a positive number is always greater than $0,$ we must have\n\n$$\n3^{8-x} > 0\n$$\n\nfor all values of $x.$\n\nTherefore, the inequality $3^{8-x} > -3$ is satisfied for all real values of $x.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
